title: Java Keystore Certificate Expiry
agents: linux
author: Felix Kraus (https://github.com/fxkraus)
catalog: os/security
license: MIT
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors certificate expiry in Java keystores ({JKS}) and
 {PKCS12} keystores using the {keytool} command-line utility.

 The agent plugin reads a configuration file that specifies one or more
 keystores to monitor, each with its password, the path to the {keytool}
 binary, and which certificate aliases to check (or all).

 For each configured keystore, the plugin reports the remaining validity
 (in days) of every monitored certificate. Warning and critical thresholds
 can be configured via WATO rules.

 The check goes {CRIT} for expired certificates and for certificates
 whose remaining validity is below the critical threshold. It goes {WARN}
 when the remaining validity is below the warning threshold.

 The plugin must be deployed to the agent's {plugins} directory, along
 with a {keystore.cfg} configuration file in the agent's config directory.
 Both can be deployed automatically through the Agent Bakery.

inventory:
 One service {Keystore <path>} is created for each keystore path found
 in the agent output.
